"""Curated verbatim repairs for ``official_eu_ai_act.OFFICIAL_ARTICLE_TEXT``.

``official_eu_ai_act.py`` is AUTOGENERATED by
``scripts/fetch_official_eu_ai_act.py`` from the EUR-Lex Cellar. The
fetch/parse occasionally drops structure that the live regulation
carries — most notably **leading paragraph numbers** and the final
"binding in its entirety" clause. Editing the autogenerated module by
hand is fragile (the next re-fetch overwrites it), so confirmed-correct
verbatim repairs live HERE and are merged on top at read time by
:mod:`app.data.provision_text`.

Each entry is the **complete, verbatim** EUR-Lex text for the keyed
provision (title prefix included, matching the autogenerated module's
shape) — never a paraphrase. Provenance for every repair is documented
inline so a reviewer can confirm fidelity against the Official Journal.

R94 — Article 113 repair
------------------------
The autogenerated ``OFFICIAL_ARTICLE_TEXT["Article 113"]`` rendered the
three subparagraphs WITHOUT their ``1./2./3.`` paragraph numbers and
omitted the closing "binding in its entirety" sentence. The numbering is
not a stylistic choice — the regulation itself cross-references
``Article 113(3), point (a)`` (in Article 111(2) and Article 112), which
is dispositive internal evidence that paragraph 3 exists and carries the
``(a)(b)(c)`` points. Article 111 and every other numbered article in
the same pinned corpus DO preserve their ``1./2./3.`` markers, so 113 is
a per-article fetch glitch, not a rendering convention. This repair
restores the numbering and appends the closing clause; the substantive
``(a)(b)(c)`` text is byte-identical to the autogenerated value.

Source: Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, Article 113 (CELEX 32024R1689),
Official Journal L series, 12 July 2024.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

OFFICIAL_TEXT_PATCHES: dict[str, str] = {
    "Article 113": (
        "Entry into force and application "
        "1. This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day "
        "following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the "
        "European Union. "
        "2. It shall apply from 2 August 2026. "
        "3. However: "
        "(a) Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025; "
        "(b) Chapter III Section 4, Chapter V, Chapter VII and Chapter XII "
        "and Article 78 shall apply from 2 August 2025, with the exception "
        "of Article 101; "
        "(c) Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations in this "
        "Regulation shall apply from 2 August 2027. "
        "This Regulation shall be binding in its entirety and directly "
        "applicable in all Member States."
    ),
}

__all__ = ["OFFICIAL_TEXT_PATCHES"]
